# Every module's build output at any depth, with source trees carved back
# out: a bare `build/` matches at every depth too, and it silently ignored a
# test placed in a `…/bangnidraw/build/` package — the file simply never
# entered a commit, while everything referring to it looked fine. Anchoring
# to one level instead would have un-ignored a nested module's output, which
# is the same silent-wrong-VCS-state failure inverted.
#
# The negation names the directory rather than files inside it, which is what
# makes it work: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a
# negation for its contents would not take, but re-including the directory
# itself does. Verified at depth: `feature/login/build/` ignored,
# `app/src/test/java/pkg/build/T.kt` tracked.
**/build/
!**/src/**/build/
dist/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
local.properties
.vscode/
captures/
.DS_Store

# IntelliJ: the project files are committed on purpose (the maintainer
# works from IDEA); .idea/.gitignore keeps the per-user ones out.

# Real signing keys must never be committed. The checked-in app/debug.keystore
# is a deliberate exception (zero-secret CI signing, docs/decisions/0005).
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
!app/debug.keystore
